(task (id "1854b55d") (title "Type checker hangs on a type error in a large recursive group or a closed-row callback instead of reporting it") (state "done") (priority 2) (assignee "") (labels "checker" "bug") (parent "") (details "Bisected while writing jsgen.deus: (1) closed-row {IO} callbacks passed where {Throw Text | r} is expected; (2) a let-bound function used at two rows; (3) a ++/:: precedence type error in a big recursive group. Each made deus compile deus run for minutes instead of reporting; deus add into a scratch codebase reports the same errors fast.") (links) (comments (comment "claude" "Cause: JIT replays (D113). A type error throws from deep inside the checker's List.forEach callback, so each group's forEach replayed. Fixed in the kernel: with a type error in Print.printer, deus compile deus reports it in 6 s instead of 78 s." (at "1792021102370810000"))))
