(task (id "62f3f4d0") (title "Names that share a hash keep only the last name's doc, comments and parameter names") (state "todo") (priority 2) (assignee "") (labels "codebase" "bug") (parent "") (details "Core has no types or names, so two definitions with the same body share a hash and one metadata file. Codebase.store keeps the newest doc, lead comments and locals (D116 merges only the scheme), so updating deus/wasm.deus gives Prove.lambdas the doc of Wasm.unlam, and view, export and the explorer print it under both names. Workaround: deus update deus/prove.deus afterwards. Proposed fix: keep name-specific fields per name when they differ, as (for \"<fqn>\" doc lead locals…) entries in the shared meta, written by mergeMeta from the batch's fqn, and read through one Codebase.metaFor meta name used by view, export, the explorer and bindings. Found by the native thread, 2026-10-14.") (links (def "Codebase.mergeMeta" (ref "20fb7353e5ff6ac38a495ad924426523b1999fccd6d29c8edcdce8df3afa9df0"))) (comments))
