(task (id "c62198a1") (title "Toolchain R2 codebase mistypes pattern variables: deus update of a match on some g fails there") (state "done") (priority 2) (assignee "") (labels "codebase" "bug") (parent "") (details "In a codebase pulled from origin.main #102beac5d7, deus add of 'def tt (h : Text) (xs : List Int) : Int := match List.head? xs with | some g => g + 1 | none => 0' fails with 'type mismatch: Int vs List Int'; it adds cleanly to a fresh init and to a restore of the git export. Updating deus/cgen.deus fails the same way at CGen.binders. Until fixed, threads update from the git export and cannot push to R2.") (links (change "1883dc98b6f8eb8c8bb6f795be6323ac985c7222829f1b112e06c9eea13ae5c7")) (comments (comment "claude" "Cause: bundles never carried the builtin objects (#List, #Option…), so a pulled store had none and the checker typed every constructor pattern as unknown, binding no subpattern and shifting later variables onto earlier slots. Fixed in D112: closureOf adds the builtins, import accepts one only as a declaration of its own identity where none is held, and unknown constructors bind every subpattern. The R2 remote now holds the builtins." (at "1792018902312206000"))))
