(task (id "f4afc2c0") (title "Metadata changes on known hashes never replicate: push sends meta only with missing objects, import keeps the first") (state "todo") (priority 2) (assignee "") (labels "replication" "spec" "codebase" "bug") (parent "") (details "Follow-up to D96: spec prose is block metadata; Replicate writes meta only when absent.") (links (def "Replicate.import" (ref "cbbdb9bbaa4ca8803f4f1a7fbcb7de6bfca18560c737a6635870d5afda89ac3e"))) (comments (comment "claude" "Seen 2026-10-14 by the native thread: a fresh clone of r2://agent-artifacts/deus/toolchain (origin.main #9db52bfe04) exports specs/JsGen.Spec.mdl with R-3's prose under the wrong blocks; the long-lived store and the git export are right. Cause: Replicate.push bundles meta only for objects the remote lacks, and Replicate.import writes meta only where none exists, so a meta-only change (spec prose, docs, D116 schemes) never reaches the remote, and a clone keeps whichever bundle it imports first. A local deus update cannot repair R2. Proposed fix: make a metadata change a content-addressed object (metaset hash form) that the causal node of the change references, so it replicates and compacts like any object, and apply metasets in causal order on merge (descendant wins; concurrent ones merge as Codebase.mergeMeta does). Subsumes 4c9147ce. Until then, export only from a long-lived store and diff codebase/specs against git before committing an export." (at "1792021680085473000"))))
